/*!
@defgroup adc
@ingroup mod_analog Analog-to-Digital Converter (ADC)
@brief Multi-mode SAR ADC module for analog sampling, sequencing, and watchdog monitoring.

@details
The ADC module converts external analog inputs into digital samples using a
successive-approximation (SAR) engine. The driver exposes configuration APIs
for converter timing, trigger selection, scan sequences, DMA handoff, result
FIFO access, and analog watchdog monitoring.

The exact feature set depends on the target device. Optional capabilities such
as injected conversions, multiple watchdog channels, second sample-time
registers, and low-power-keep behavior are enabled through `FEATURE_ADC_*`
macros in the device-specific feature headers.

@section adc_features Key Features
- Selectable conversion resolution: 12-bit, 10-bit, 8-bit, or 6-bit.
- Configurable startup time, sample time, and input clock divider.
- Software-triggered or hardware-triggered conversion flow.
- Sequence conversion modes for step, loop, and continuous scanning.
- Result FIFO with DMA watermark support.
- Analog watchdog compare window for threshold monitoring.
- Optional injected conversion path on supported devices.
- Polled status APIs for conversion completion, end-of-sequence, ready, sample-end,
  overrun, and watchdog events.

@section adc_modes Supported Modes

@subsection adc_modes_resolution Resolution Modes
| Mode | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `ADC_RESOLUTION_12BIT` | Highest conversion precision. |
| `ADC_RESOLUTION_10BIT` | Reduced conversion width for faster processing or smaller result range. |
| `ADC_RESOLUTION_8BIT` | Compact conversion result for lightweight sampling paths. |
| `ADC_RESOLUTION_6BIT` | Lowest conversion width with the smallest result range. |

@subsection adc_modes_trigger Trigger Modes
| Mode | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `ADC_TRIGGER_SOFTWARE` | Start conversion through software control. |
| `ADC_TRIGGER_HARDWARE` | Start conversion from the configured hardware trigger source. |
| `ADC_TRIG_INJECT_*` | Combined normal/injected trigger selection on devices that support injection mode. |

@subsection adc_modes_sequence Sequence Modes
| Mode | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `ADC_CONV_STEP` | Convert one configured channel per trigger event. |
| `ADC_CONV_LOOP` | Convert the full configured sequence for each trigger event. |
| `ADC_CONV_CONTINUOUS` | Continuously restart sequence conversion after each trigger launch. |

@section adc_arch Module Architecture

The ADC module uses a two-layer software structure:

@verbatim
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              Application Code                │
│         (calls ADC_DRV_* functions)          │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│           ADC Driver Layer                   │
│  ● Configuration structure helpers           │
│  ● Converter / sequence / watchdog APIs      │
│  ● Runtime control, polling, and FIFO reads  │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│         ADC HW Access Layer                  │
│  ● Inline register access helpers            │
│  ● Timing / trigger / DMA configuration      │
│  ● Sequence, interrupt, and flag control     │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│           ADC Peripheral Hardware            │
│  ● CTRL / CFG / STS / FIFO / CHSEL           │
│  ● Watchdog threshold and interrupt logic    │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
@endverbatim

@subsection adc_arch_driver Driver Layer (`adc_driver.h` / `adc_driver.c`)
Application code should call the `ADC_DRV_*` APIs. The driver converts
instance numbers into base addresses, applies configuration structures, and
provides higher-level runtime helpers such as polling, FIFO access, and flag
management.

@subsection adc_arch_hw HW Access Layer (`adc_hw_access.h`)
The hardware access layer exposes low-level inline helpers that directly read
or write ADC registers. These helpers are grouped by converter control,
hardware compare, sequence configuration, interrupt/flag management, and FIFO
runtime operations.

@section adc_config Configuration Parameters

@subsection adc_config_converter adc_converter_config_t Fields
| Field | Type | Description | Default |
|------|------|-------------|---------|
| `clockDivider` | `adc_clk_divide_t` | ADC input clock divider. | `ADC_DEFAULT_CLOCK_DIVIDER` |
| `startTime` | `uint8_t` | Startup delay in ADC clock cycles. | `ADC_DEFAULT_START_TIME` |
| `sampleTime` | `uint8_t` | Primary sample time in ADC clock cycles. | `ADC_DEFAULT_SAMPLE_TIME` |
| `overrunMode` | `bool` | Overwrite FIFO data on overrun when enabled. | `false` |
| `autoOffEnable` | `bool` | Automatically power down the converter between conversions. | `false` |
| `waitEnable` | `bool` | Stall conversion when the result FIFO is full. | `false` |
| `triggerSource` | `uint8_t` | Hardware trigger source selector. | `0` |
| `trigger` | `adc_trigger_t` | Software/hardware trigger mode selection. | Software-trigger default |
| `align` | `adc_align_t` | Result alignment in the FIFO/register view. | Right-aligned default |
| `resolution` | `adc_resolution_t` | Conversion result width. | `ADC_RESOLUTION_12BIT` |
| `dmaWaterMark` | `uint8_t` | FIFO watermark level used by DMA requests. | `1` |
| `dmaEnable` | `bool` | Enable DMA requests from the result FIFO. | `false` |
| `sequenceConfig` | `adc_sequence_config_t` | Normal conversion sequence settings. | Single-channel loop sequence |
| `injectConfig` | `adc_inject_config_t` | Injected conversion settings on supported devices. | Disabled |
| `compareConfig` / `adcCompareCnt` | `adc_compare_config_t` / `uint8_t` | Analog watchdog settings. | Disabled |

@subsection adc_config_sequence adc_sequence_config_t Fields
| Field | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `channels[]` | `adc_inputchannel_t[]` | Ordered list of input channels for the normal sequence. |
| `totalChannels` | `uint8_t` | Number of active sequence entries. |
| `sequenceMode` | `adc_sequence_mode_t` | Step, loop, or continuous scan behavior. |
| `sequenceIntEnable` | `bool` | Enable end-of-sequence interrupt generation. |
| `convIntEnable` | `bool` | Enable end-of-conversion interrupt generation. |
| `ovrunIntEnable` | `bool` | Enable FIFO overrun interrupt generation. |
| `sampIntEnable` | `bool` | Enable sample-end interrupt generation. |
| `readyIntEnable` | `bool` | Enable ADC-ready interrupt generation. |

@subsection adc_config_compare adc_compare_config_t Fields
| Field | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `compareEnable` | `bool` | Enable analog watchdog monitoring. |
| `compareAllChannelEnable` | `bool` | Apply watchdog monitoring to all channels when supported. |
| `compChalSel` | `adc_inputchannel_t` | Input channel monitored by the watchdog. |
| `compHigh` | `uint16_t` | Upper threshold (always expressed in 12-bit scale). |
| `compLow` | `uint16_t` | Lower threshold (always expressed in 12-bit scale). |
| `compIntEnable` | `bool` | Enable watchdog interrupt reporting. |
| `effectiveMode` | `adc_awg_effective_mode_t` | Select inside-window or outside-window match behavior. |

@subsection adc_config_features Device Feature Macros
| Macro | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `FEATURE_ADC_SUPPORT_INJECTION_MODE` | Indicates whether injected conversions are available. |
| `FEATURE_ADC_WDG_CHANNEL_COUNT` | Number of watchdog channels implemented by the hardware. |
| `FEATURE_ADC_SUPPORT_SECOND_SMP` | Indicates whether the converter exposes a second sample-time field. |
| `FEATURE_ADC_SUPPORT_LOW_POWER_KEEP` | Indicates whether low-power keep control is available. |
| `FEATURE_ADC_MAX_NUM_EXT_CHANS` | Maximum number of external analog input channels. |

@section adc_usage Usage Patterns

@subsection adc_usage_basic Pattern 1: Basic Single-Channel Conversion
@code{.c}
#define INST_ADC (0U)

adc_converter_config_t converterConfig;

ADC_DRV_InitConverterStruct(&converterConfig);
converterConfig.sequenceConfig.channels[0] = ADC_INPUTCHAN_EXT0;
converterConfig.sequenceConfig.totalChannels = 1U;
converterConfig.sequenceConfig.sequenceMode = ADC_CONV_LOOP;

ADC_DRV_ConfigConverter(INST_ADC, &converterConfig);
ADC_DRV_Enable(INST_ADC);
ADC_DRV_Start(INST_ADC);
ADC_DRV_WaitConvDone(INST_ADC);

uint16_t sample = ADC_DRV_ReadFIFO(INST_ADC);

ADC_DRV_Stop(INST_ADC);
ADC_DRV_Disable(INST_ADC);
@endcode

@subsection adc_usage_watchdog Pattern 2: Analog Watchdog Monitoring
@code{.c}
#define INST_ADC (0U)

adc_compare_config_t compareConfig;

ADC_DRV_InitHwCompareStruct(&compareConfig);
compareConfig.compareEnable = true;
compareConfig.compChalSel = ADC_INPUTCHAN_EXT0;
compareConfig.compLow = 0x0200U;
compareConfig.compHigh = 0x0C00U;
compareConfig.compIntEnable = true;
compareConfig.effectiveMode = ADC_AWG_EFFECTIVE_OUTSIDE;

ADC_DRV_ConfigHwCompare(INST_ADC, &compareConfig);

if (ADC_DRV_GetWatchdogFlag(INST_ADC))
{
    ADC_DRV_ClearWdFlagCmd(INST_ADC);
}
@endcode

@subsection adc_usage_sequence Pattern 3: Sequence Conversion with FIFO Readout
@code{.c}
#define INST_ADC (0U)

adc_sequence_config_t sequenceConfig;

ADC_DRV_InitSequenceStruct(&sequenceConfig);
sequenceConfig.channels[0] = ADC_INPUTCHAN_EXT0;
sequenceConfig.channels[1] = ADC_INPUTCHAN_EXT1;
sequenceConfig.totalChannels = 2U;
sequenceConfig.sequenceMode = ADC_CONV_LOOP;
sequenceConfig.sequenceIntEnable = true;

ADC_DRV_ConfigSequence(INST_ADC, &sequenceConfig);
ADC_DRV_Start(INST_ADC);
ADC_DRV_WaitSequenceDone(INST_ADC);

uint32_t taggedResult = ADC_DRV_ReadSeqtagAndData(INST_ADC);
ADC_DRV_ClearEoseqFlagCmd(INST_ADC);
@endcode

@subsection adc_usage_dma Pattern 4: DMA-Oriented Converter Setup
@code{.c}
#define INST_ADC (0U)

adc_converter_config_t converterConfig;

ADC_DRV_InitConverterStruct(&converterConfig);
converterConfig.dmaEnable = true;
converterConfig.dmaWaterMark = 4U;
converterConfig.waitEnable = true;

ADC_DRV_ConfigConverter(INST_ADC, &converterConfig);
@endcode

@section adc_api API Quick Reference

@subsection adc_api_converter Converter Configuration
| Function | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `ADC_DRV_InitConverterStruct()` | Fill the converter configuration structure with safe defaults. |
| `ADC_DRV_ConfigConverter()` | Apply top-level converter, sequence, DMA, and watchdog settings. |
| `ADC_DRV_GetConverterConfig()` | Read back the active converter configuration. |

@subsection adc_api_compare Hardware Compare
| Function | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `ADC_DRV_InitHwCompareStruct()` | Fill the analog watchdog configuration structure with defaults. |
| `ADC_DRV_ConfigHwCompare()` | Apply a single watchdog configuration. |
| `ADC_DRV_ConfigHwCompareGroup()` | Apply a watchdog configuration array on devices with multiple channels. |
| `ADC_DRV_GetHwCompareConfig()` | Read back watchdog configuration data. |

@subsection adc_api_sequence Sequence Configuration
| Function | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `ADC_DRV_InitSequenceStruct()` | Fill the sequence configuration structure with default values. |
| `ADC_DRV_ConfigSequence()` | Program the normal conversion sequence. |
| `ADC_DRV_GetSequenceConfig()` | Read back the normal conversion sequence state. |
| `ADC_DRV_ConfigInject()` | Program the injected conversion sequence on supported devices. |
| `ADC_DRV_GetInjectConfig()` | Read back the injected conversion sequence state. |

@subsection adc_api_runtime Runtime Control and Status
| Function | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `ADC_DRV_Reset()` | Restore the converter to its reset-style runtime state. |
| `ADC_DRV_Enable()` | Enable the ADC hardware. |
| `ADC_DRV_Disable()` | Disable the ADC hardware and abort active work. |
| `ADC_DRV_Start()` | Launch or arm conversion according to the trigger mode. |
| `ADC_DRV_Stop()` | Stop the current conversion activity. |
| `ADC_DRV_WaitConvDone()` | Poll until the current conversion is no longer active. |
| `ADC_DRV_WaitSequenceDone()` | Poll until the configured sequence completes. |
| `ADC_DRV_ReadFIFO()` | Read one conversion result from the FIFO. |
| `ADC_DRV_ReadSeqtagAndData()` | Read a tagged FIFO entry that includes sequence metadata. |

@subsection adc_api_flags Flag and Interrupt Utilities
| Function | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `ADC_DRV_GetConvCompleteFlag()` | Report the conversion-complete flag state. |
| `ADC_DRV_GetEndOfConversionFlag()` | Report the end-of-conversion flag state. |
| `ADC_DRV_GetFullOfConversionFlag()` | Report whether the result FIFO is full. |
| `ADC_DRV_GetOvrRunOfConversionFlag()` | Report whether a FIFO overrun occurred. |
| `ADC_DRV_GetWatchdogFlag()` | Report watchdog threshold events. |
| `ADC_DRV_GetEndOfSequenceFlag()` | Report end-of-sequence status. |
| `ADC_DRV_GetReadyFlag()` | Report ADC-ready status. |
| `ADC_DRV_GetSampEndFlag()` | Report sample-end status. |
| `ADC_DRV_GetInterruptNumber()` | Return the IRQ number associated with an ADC instance. |
| `ADC_DRV_ClearWdFlagCmd()` | Clear the watchdog flag. |
| `ADC_DRV_ClearReadyFlagCmd()` | Clear the ready flag. |
| `ADC_DRV_ClearSampEndFlagCmd()` | Clear the sample-end flag. |
| `ADC_DRV_ClearOvrFlagCmd()` | Clear the overrun flag. |
| `ADC_DRV_ClearEoseqFlagCmd()` | Clear the end-of-sequence flag. |
| `ADC_DRV_ClearEocFlagCmd()` | Clear the end-of-conversion flag. |

@section adc_notes Important Notes

@subsection adc_notes_clock Clock and Pin Dependencies
The ADC driver does not enable clocks or configure I/O pins. The ADC peripheral
clock and the selected analog input pins must be configured before calling the
driver APIs. See @ref clock_manager and the PORT/pin-mux configuration flow
used by the application.

@subsection adc_notes_sequence Sequence Reconfiguration
`ADC_DRV_ConfigSequence()` and `ADC_DRV_ConfigInject()` stop the ADC before
rewriting sequence registers. Reconfiguring a live sequence therefore aborts
the active conversion in progress.

@subsection adc_notes_watchdog Watchdog Threshold Encoding
The watchdog low/high thresholds are programmed in the hardware watchdog
threshold registers using the ADC's 12-bit scaling convention. Keep this in
mind when using lower conversion resolutions.

@subsection adc_notes_fifo FIFO and Flag Handling
- Read FIFO results often enough to avoid `OVR` overrun conditions.
- Clear sticky status flags with the dedicated `ADC_DRV_Clear*FlagCmd()`
  helpers before re-entering the same polling loop.
- When `waitEnable` is set, conversions may stall until FIFO space becomes
  available.

@subsection adc_notes_device Device Variations
Some APIs and structure fields are compiled only when their matching feature
macros are enabled. Review the device-specific feature header before relying on
injected conversion support, multiple watchdog channels, or alternate sample
timing fields.

@section adc_integration Integration Guide

@subsection adc_integration_units Compilation Units
Compile the following source file into the project:

@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/adc/adc_driver.c
@endverbatim

@subsection adc_integration_include Include Path
Add the public driver include directory to the compiler include search path:

@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/inc/
@endverbatim

@subsection adc_integration_symbols Compile Symbols
No module-specific compile symbols are required beyond the device selection
macros already used by the SDK.

@subsection adc_integration_deps Dependencies
- @ref clock_manager
- Device feature headers pulled in through `device_registers.h`

*/
